  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'm attempting to make VR-OSC function in VRChat. It does function, but a significant glitch prevents me from using it: activating the OSC option in the in-game Wheel Menu immediately causes issues with my avatar.\n\nWhen I enable the OSC option, my field of view becomes confined within the avatar, causing me to see the avatar from the inside and losing control over it.\n\nIf I restart the game with the OSC option enabled, my avatar simply becomes invisible or disappears.\n\nBoth of these glitches are resolved only when I disable the OSC option and reload an avatar.\n\nAdditionally, I've observed that the \"Expressions\" sub-menu becomes frozen or disabled when the OSC option is enabled, which might be related? I'm unsure.\n\nCould you assist me in resolving this problem?\n\nSystem Information: I'm a PC-VR player using Quest 2 + \"Virtual Desktop\" on SteamVR (Windows 11).\n\n[SOLVED] It appears that the issue was caused by something else I did to the VRChat folder a few days ago. To save space on my C disk, I created a Symbolic Link in the original folder and moved the actual folder to the D disk, where I have more available space.\n\nHowever, this setup prevented the VRChat app from creating new files in the actual folder, which was the root cause of the problem I reported here. Once I moved the folder back to its original location, the bug was resolved. Thanks for the assistance, regardless!",
